 "_about": "Public-domain Carl Friedrich Keil (1807-1888), Lutheran Old Testament scholar of Dorpat and Leipzig, for the Word Hoard: his volumes of the Keil and Delitzsch Biblical Commentary on the Old Testament (Pentateuch, Joshua-Judges-Ruth, Samuel, Kings, Chronicles, Ezra-Nehemiah-Esther, Jeremiah and Lamentations, Ezekiel, Daniel, the Twelve Minor Prophets), his Introduction to the Old Testament and his Manual of Biblical Archaeology, all in the English translations of Clark's Foreign Theological Library (Edinburgh, 1864-1888), from Internet Archive scans. Delitzsch's own volumes of the same series are on the franz-delitzsch shelf. Added 2026-10-23 by lane A, round 48 (my pick); Adam may veto the whole shelf. Every printing dated before 1930, so public domain in the US. No uids minted.",
